# Trivy ignore list for fulmen-toolbox runner / sbom-tools images.
#
# Add CVEs here only with rationale and a date. Format:
#   <CVE-ID>  # YYYY-MM-DD: <rationale>; review by YYYY-MM-DD
#
# This file is read by the cve-scan workflow and by `make precommit` (trivy
# scan of Dockerfile sources). Keep entries minimal and time-boxed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADMISSION RULE: an entry belongs here only if the fix is genuinely out of our
# reach — the fix exists in a dependency, but no upstream release of the tool we
# ship carries it yet, AND we are already on that tool's latest release.
# "We haven't gotten to it" is not a rationale; bump the pin instead.
#
# EVERY entry below was verified against the v0.5.0 build (2026-07-30) by
# scanning the actual images with the shipped trivy v0.72.0 and attributing each
# finding to the binary carrying it. Do not carry an entry forward on trust —
# re-scan WITHOUT this file and drop anything that no longer appears. Two
# concrete precedents: the v0.5.0 sweep dropped eight yq stdlib entries whose
# rationale had gone stale, and this revision dropped CVE-2026-33671 (picomatch)
# because updating the pinned npm cleared it outright.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Go stdlib embedded in PREBUILT upstream binaries ------------------------
# syft and grype ship as anchore's official signed release binaries, not built
# by us, so we inherit the Go toolchain anchore compiled with. Both v1.50.0 and
# v0.116.1 — the newest releases as of 2026-07-30 — are built with go1.26.3
# (verified via `go version -m` on the downloaded release artifacts). These
# clear when anchore rebuilds on go1.26.4+ / go1.26.5+.
#
# The alternative is building syft/grype from source with our own Go 1.26.5,
# which would clear all three. That trades away anchore's signed upstream
# provenance and is a deliberate posture change, not a pin bump — deferred, not
# forgotten.
CVE-2026-27145  # 2026-07-30: stdlib in prebuilt syft v1.50.0 / grype v0.116.1 (go1.26.3); fixed in go1.26.4; on-latest-upstream; review by 2026-10-30
CVE-2026-42504  # 2026-07-30: stdlib in prebuilt syft v1.50.0 / grype v0.116.1 (go1.26.3); fixed in go1.26.4; on-latest-upstream; review by 2026-10-30
CVE-2026-39822  # 2026-07-30: stdlib in prebuilt syft/grype (go1.26.3) plus trivy v0.72.0 and yq v4.53.3 (both go1.26.4); needs go1.26.5; all three on latest release; review by 2026-10-30

# --- golang.org/x/text in prebuilt / upstream-pinned binaries ----------------
# Three distinct carriers, none of which we can move:
#   golangci-lint v2.12.1 -> x/text v0.36.0. We DO build this from source, so
#     the version comes from its own go.mod, not our toolchain. v2.12.2 (latest)
#     ships the identical v0.36.0 — verified via `go version -m` — so bumping
#     would not clear this finding.
#   yq v4.53.3 (latest) -> x/text v0.37.0.
#   trivy v0.72.0 (latest) -> x/text v0.38.0.
# Fixed in x/text v0.39.0; clears as each upstream bumps its dependency.
CVE-2026-56852  # 2026-07-30: x/text in golangci-lint v2.12.1 (v0.36.0), yq v4.53.3 (v0.37.0), trivy v0.72.0 (v0.38.0); fixed in v0.39.0; v2.12.2 verified to carry the same v0.36.0; review by 2026-10-30

# --- Vendored dependencies in prebuilt upstream binaries ---------------------
# grype vendors github.com/docker/docker v28.5.2 (fixed in v29.3.1). Re-verified
# 2026-07-30 against v0.116.1, the newest release — the dependency is unchanged
# from v0.116.0, so the version bump taken this cycle did not clear it.
CVE-2026-34040  # 2026-07-30: grype v0.116.1 vendors docker/docker v28.5.2; fixed in 29.3.1; on-latest-upstream; review by 2026-10-30

# trivy v0.72.0 (latest, 2026-06-30) vendors oras-go v2.6.0 and grpc v1.81.0.
# Note the asymmetry worth remembering: syft/grype v1.50.0/v0.116.1 DO carry the
# fixed grpc v1.82.1, which is why the goneat runners are clear of the grpc
# finding while the sbom images — which additionally ship trivy — are not.
# Same CVE, different carrier.
CVE-2026-50151      # 2026-07-30: trivy v0.72.0 vendors oras-go v2.6.0; fixed in 2.6.1; on-latest-upstream; sbom-tools images only; review by 2026-10-30
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf # 2026-07-30: trivy v0.72.0 vendors grpc v1.81.0; fixed in 1.82.1; on-latest-upstream; sbom-tools images only (syft/grype already carry the fixed 1.82.1); review by 2026-10-30

# --- Bundled npm dependency tree --------------------------------------------
# We pin npm to 12.0.1 (see the npm stage in the goneat Dockerfiles), which
# cleared CRITICAL CVE-2026-59873 (tar) plus CVE-2026-59874, CVE-2026-48815
# (sigstore), CVE-2026-13149 (brace-expansion) and CVE-2026-33671 (picomatch).
# npm 12.0.1 bundles brace-expansion 5.0.7; this advisory needs 5.0.8, which no
# published npm release ships yet. Clears on the next npm that bundles it — at
# which point the pin bump closes this without further work.
CVE-2026-14257  # 2026-07-30: brace-expansion 5.0.7 bundled inside pinned npm 12.0.1; fixed in 5.0.8; no npm release ships 5.0.8 yet; goneat-tools images only; review by 2026-10-30
